", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "JER.47.4.a021", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.4.021"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.4.021", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "JER.47.4.a022", "note": "The explicit subject Jehovah is aligned separately.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.4.022"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.4.022", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t025", "t026"], "target_head": "t026"}, {"id": "JER.47.4.a023", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.4.023"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.4.023", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024"], "target_head": "t024"}, {"id": "JER.47.4.a024", "note": "The direct-object marker has no separate English realization.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.4.024"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.4.024", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JER.47.4.a025", "note": "The supplied definite article belongs to the articleless gentilic noun.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.4.025"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.4.025", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t027", "t028"], "target_head": "t028"}, {"id": "JER.47.4.a026", "note": "The supplied definite article belongs to the construct noun.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.4.026"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.4.026", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t029", "t030"], "target_head": "t030"}, {"id": "JER.47.4.a027", "note": "As the nomen rectum, this noun takes the construct relation 'of' and a supplied definite article.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.4.027"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.4.027", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t031", "t032", "t033"], "target_head": "t033"}, {"id": "JER.47.4.a028", "note": "The final nomen rectum takes the construct relation 'of'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.4.028"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.4.028", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t034", "t035"], "target_head": "t035"}], "ref": "JER.47.4", "review_notes": ["The ASV margin offers 'sea-coast' for 'isle'; the alignment follows the printed main-text rendering."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JER.47.5.a001", "note": "The explicit subject 'Baldness' is aligned separately.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JER.47.5.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JER.47.5.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JER.47.5.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JER.47.5.a005", "note": "The verb is rendered by the result phrase 'is brought to nought'; 'nought' carries the lexical force.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t008", "t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JER.47.5.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JER.47.5.a007", "note": "The supplied definite article belongs to the construct noun.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "JER.47.5.a008", "note": "As the nomen rectum, the noun takes the construct relation 'of'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013", "t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JER.47.5.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JER.47.5.a010", "note": "In the idiomatic question, עַד supplies the durative force rendered 'long'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "JER.47.5.a011", "note": "The interrogative is rendered 'how' in the phrase 'how long'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JER.47.5.a012", "note": "The reflexive pronoun renders the source verb's reflexive stem and remains in the verb's unit.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.5.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.5.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018", "t019", "t020", "t021"], "target_head": "t020"}], "ref": "JER.47.5", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JER.47.6.a001", "note": "The interjection is rendered 'O'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a002", "note": "The vocative noun takes the supplied 'thou'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a005", "note": "I treated עַד אָנָה and the ASV frame 'how long will it be' as one indivisible temporal-interrogative expression, following the exact recasting in HOS.8.5; the atomized 'how'/'long' reading used where no matrix frame intervenes remains possible, but would leave 'will it be' without a uniquely defensible internal owner here.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.005", "WLC.JER.47.6.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.005", "status": "noncompositional", "target": ["t006", "t007", "t008", "t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a006", "note": "The ASV recasts the Hebrew negation as the prospective conjunction 'ere'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a007", "note": "The finite verb takes the subordinate subject and predicate 'thou be quiet'; the matrix duration frame belongs to the preceding temporal-interrogative expression.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013", "t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a008", "note": "'Up' is a phrasal particle, and 'thyself' renders the verb's reflexive voice.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015", "t016", "t017"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a009", "note": "The prepared token metadata conflicts: its surface, gloss, and morph look negative, while its lemma, Strong's number, translation evidence, and context identify the directional preposition אֶל. Following the prepared lexical identity without making a new textual decision, I aligned the ASV's 'into'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a013", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.014"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "JER.47.6.a014", "note": "The light copular rendering heads on the lexical complement 'still'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.6.015"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.6.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023", "t024"], "target_head": "t024"}], "ref": "JER.47.6", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JER.47.7.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a002", "note": "Because the interrogative has its own word, the fronted modal remains with the finite verb.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003", "t004", "t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a003", "note": "The ASV renders this waw by the causal connective 'seeing'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a005", "note": "The verb is rendered by the discontinuous light-verb phrase 'hath given ... a charge'; 'charge' carries the lexeme.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008", "t009", "t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a006", "note": "The dative preposition has no separate English word in the recasting 'given thee a charge'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.006", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a007", "note": "The suffix is rendered by the indirect-object pronoun 'thee'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a012", "note": "The construct noun is rendered attributively as 'shore' after its nomen rectum.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a013", "note": "The nomen rectum's article takes the phrase-initial English 'the'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a014", "note": "The nomen rectum is rendered attributively as 'sea'.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.014"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.015"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a016", "note": "The finite verb takes its subject pronoun and auxiliary; its object suffix is aligned separately.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.016"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021", "t022", "t023"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "JER.47.7.a017", "note": "The suffix is rendered by 'it,' as also indicated by the ASV Hebrew note.", "source": ["WLC.JER.47.7.017"], "source_head": "WLC.JER.47.7.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024"], "target_head": "t024"}], "ref": "JER.47.7", "review_notes": ["The ASV note identifies the final pronominal object as Hebrew 'it'."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
